From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Retry WM reader sample reads interrupted by flushing.

Colin McRae Rally 3 switches stream formats while an asynchronous WM reader
worker is waiting for a sample from frontend.wmv. Reinitialization wakes
the worker with S_FALSE, the packet queue's internal flush/retry result.
GetNextSample currently passes that result through without returning an
INSSBuffer. The async reader accepts the successful HRESULT and queues a
null buffer, then crashes releasing it while stopping the stream.

Keep the flush result internal, as the previous winegstreamer reader did.
Synchronize with reinitialization through reader->cs, then retry stream
selection and sample delivery. Do not retain this synchronization lock
across the retry's blocking read. If shutdown caused the flush, report
NS_E_NO_MORE_SAMPLES instead of retrying against the closed reader.

This fixes the producer contract rather than skipping null releases in
wmvcore, which would leave invalid samples reaching its callbacks.

Reported by DropboxKenshiro.
Bug: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/633
Log: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/633#issuecomment-5978191702
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c b/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c
index 464ba93f..ba9e539c 100644
--- a/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c
@@ -2861,6 +2861,7 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI reader_SetOutputProps(IWMSyncReader2 *iface, DWORD output,
     struct wm_reader *reader = impl_from_IWMSyncReader2(iface);
     struct output_props *props = unsafe_impl_from_IWMOutputMediaProps(props_iface);
     struct winedmo_codec_format format;
+retry:
     struct wm_stream *stream;
     HRESULT hr = S_OK;
     int i;
@@ -2947,6 +2948,19 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI reader_SetOutputSetting(IWMSyncReader2 *iface, DWORD outpu
         FIXME("Ignoring EnableDiscreteOutput setting.\n");
         return S_OK;
     }
+    if (hr == S_FALSE)
+    {
+        /* Flushing does not produce a sample. Wait for reinitialization under
+         * reader->cs before retrying, without holding it across a blocking read. */
+        if (!reader_locked)
+            EnterCriticalSection(&reader->cs);
+        hr = reader->demux_shutdown ? NS_E_NO_MORE_SAMPLES : S_FALSE;
+        LeaveCriticalSection(&reader->cs);
+        reader_locked = FALSE;
+        if (hr == S_FALSE)
+            goto retry;
+    }
+
     if (!wcscmp(name, L"SpeakerConfig"))
     {
         FIXME("Ignoring SpeakerConfig setting.\n");
